I think floating eyes and water/wood/... nymphs also are major indirect
causes for death (though unlike traps more likely due to player stupidity
or intentional risk taking).

Running into (or attacking on purpose) a floating eye freezes you while
some low level monster finishes you off ('killed by a newt').

Or a nymph steals your only weapon/only good armor and you get killed by 
monsters which you otherwise could have managed easily.

Also, monsters capable of using a wand should be a more probable source
of death than those with comparable stats but unable to use wands. Ever
been zapped to death with those wands of magic missile/fire/cold/death 
that that #@$% gnome found before you did?

